.TH TUXDISPLAY-USB 8 "September 2026" "TuxDisplay 0.3.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tuxdisplay-usb \- configure optional USB gadget Ethernet for TuxDisplay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxdisplay-usb
.BR setup | teardown
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuxdisplay-usb
creates a USB CDC ECM Ethernet gadget using Linux ConfigFS, assigns 10.55.0.1/24 to the gadget interface, and starts a private DHCP service. It is intended only for computers with a USB Device Controller and a device or dual-role USB port.
.PP
Most desktop and laptop USB ports are host-only. On those computers connect and trust the iPad, enable Personal Hotspot on iPadOS, and use
.B tuxdisplay usb connect
to activate and prefer the ipheth cable address.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Create and bind the gadget, configure its network interface, and start dnsmasq.
.TP
.B teardown
Stop the private dnsmasq process, unbind the gadget, and remove only the TuxDisplay ConfigFS objects.
.SH URL
After successful setup, open
.B http://10.55.0.1:6080/
on the attached iPad.
.SH SERVICE
The disabled-by-default
.B tuxdisplay-usb-gadget.service
system unit runs this helper. Enable it only after confirming that
.I /sys/class/udc
contains a controller.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuxdisplay (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR dnsmasq (8)
